From: Jakob Kummerow <jkummerow@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:49:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [M156] [turboshaft] Bound JS stack frame size to 4KB

Original change's description:
> [turboshaft] Bound JS stack frame size to 4KB
>
> CodeGenerator::AssembleConstructFrame grows the stack frame for
> optimized JS functions (including OSR) with a single stack pointer
> decrement before the kJSFunctionEntry stack check runs. A frame larger
> than 4KB can therefore step over an OS stack guard page.
>
> Following Maglev (https://crrev.com/c/8137738), abort optimization in
> Pipeline::AllocateRegisters with BailoutReason::kFunctionTooBig when the
> total frame slot count exceeds 4KB.
>
